Answer: (C) UPDATE STUDENT Marks = 90 WHERE RollNo = 3;
Why: The UPDATE command needs the keyword SET: UPDATE STUDENT SET Marks = 90 WHERE RollNo = 3;. Without SET, it is a syntax error.
Why not the others: (A), (B) and (D) follow the correct syntax of SELECT, DELETE and ALTER TABLE.
Key point: UPDATE table SET column = value [WHERE condition];

